# Anti-Slop UI

Dense product chrome, not marketing pages. Do not apply landing section padding, 60/40 grids, or 1200px max-width to the workbench.

## Never

- Gradient backgrounds or CTAs (especially blue→purple)
- Glassmorphism / backdrop-blur, floating orbs, aurora wallpaper
- `rounded-3xl` everywhere; drop shadows on every card
- Hover effects on non-interactive elements
- Emoji in headings; decorative stock/abstract hero imagery
- Colored body text on colored backgrounds for decoration

## Defaults

- Background: solid. Radius: 4px (theme). Cards: border, not shadow (one shadow/page max)
- Palette: one accent + grays. Text: near-black / near-white on surfaces
- Hover: opacity, underline, or border — subtle. Animation: opacity + transform, ~200ms ease-out
- CTA: solid fill

## Typography

Use size, weight, case/tracking, color, and family — not size alone.

- Display: lighter (300–400). Body: 400. Labels/emphasis: 600
- Labels/eyebrows: uppercase + letter-spacing (use `.type-label`); mono for metadata/code
- Chrome may stay 14px; empty-state / readable body prefer ≥16px when space allows

## Semantic status

Tint backgrounds + icons OK. Prefer `text-foreground` / `text-muted-foreground` on tints; put semantic color on the icon. Avoid `text-warning` on `bg-warning-tint` when border + muted text works.
